# Enquiry form — Google SMTP (smtp.gmail.com, port 465).
# The site delivers nothing until both variables are set on Vercel.
# A missing value does not crash the page: the form shows the phone and email fallback.
#
# 1. On ryan@webservicesforbusiness.com, turn on 2-step verification:
#    https://myaccount.google.com/signinoptions/two-step-verification
# 2. Create an app password (name it something like "WSFB contact form"):
#    https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
#    If that page is missing, a Google Workspace admin must allow app passwords
#    for the account. Do not use the normal mailbox password.
# 3. Vercel → project webservicesforbusiness → Settings → Environment Variables
#    Add both for Production, then redeploy:
#      SMTP_USER=ryan@webservicesforbusiness.com
#      SMTP_PASS=<the 16-character app password>
#    Spaces in the app password are fine. Do not commit the password.

SMTP_USER=ryan@webservicesforbusiness.com
SMTP_PASS=
